 * This banner previously had a working dismiss button that persisted the
 * choice in localStorage. That is now removed entirely, and it is also the
 * reason the banner "never appeared" during testing: it HAD been dismissed
 * once, and a localStorage flag is permanent, so it stayed hidden on every
 * subsequent page load with no way back short of clearing site data.
 *
 * Removed rather than reworked, per instruction. What went with it:
 *   - the close <button> and its icon
 *   - the synchronous pre-paint script that read localStorage
 *   - web/js/top-banner.js (the whole widget) and its requirejs-config map
 *     entry in Spartrak_Catalog
 *   - the .spartrak-top-banner-dismissed CSS branch
 *
 * Net effect is less JS on every page, no localStorage dependency, and no
 * layout-shift risk at all — the banner is now a static block of markup.
 *
 * DELIBERATE FIGMA DEVIATION, FLAGGED: node 693:45402 draws an X at the
 * banner's inline end. It is not rendered, because a visible close button that
 * does nothing is worse than no button. If the banner should be dismissable
 * again, the right shape is a per-session dismissal (sessionStorage) or an
 * admin on/off toggle — not the permanent localStorage flag that caused this.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * CONTENT COMES FROM CODE, NOT CMS BLOCKS
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * The offer sentence and badge used to come from two Magento\Cms\Block\Block
 * children (spartrak_top_banner, spartrak_top_banner_badge). Neither static
 * block existed in the database, and this template bailed out entirely when
 * the offer block was empty — so the banner did not render at all.
 *
 * Both are now plain __() strings, per the explicit project instruction that
 * this content is handled in code. The copy is still changeable without a
 * deploy because __() strings are translatable per store view (the Arabic
 * wording lives in this theme's i18n/ar_EG.csv), and it removes two
 * static-block lookups from every page render.
 *
 * The offer sentence carries no `%` placeholder: Magento's Phrase renderer
 * treats `%` specially, so the discount figure is part of the translated
 * string rather than a substitution, which keeps the source key and the CSV
 * key byte-identical and avoids a silent no-match.
 *
 * @var \Magento\Framework\View\Element\Template $block
 */
